# Patterns here are matched with Go's filepath.Match, where `*` stops at a `/`.
# A bare `node_modules` therefore excludes only the one at the root, and every
# nested one — ui/node_modules above all — is copied into the build context.
# That is not merely wasteful: a pnpm modules directory records the store it was
# installed from, so the host's arrives in the image pointing at a store that is
# not there. pnpm then wants to purge it, asks for confirmation, finds no TTY,
# and the build dies with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY. Every
# pattern below that should apply at any depth is written `**/`.

# Dependencies
**/node_modules

# Build output (we build in Docker)
**/dist

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Environment files — supplied at run time by docker-compose
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test files
coverage
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
jest.json
tsconfig.spec.json

# Documentation
docs
**/*.md
!README.md

# Misc
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
